Hello,

In "Stepping up with GGIR: Validity of step cadence derived from wrist-worn research-grade accelerometers using the verisense step count algorithm" (https://doi.org/10.1080/02640414.2022.2147134) Rowlands refers to a second, revised, version of the step-count algorithm and gives the reference link to the upload on github (https://github.com/ShimmerEngineering/Verisense-Toolbox/tree/master/Verisense_step_algorithm).
Since this uploaded step-count algorithm has no version labeling or revision date, the question remains:
Is the uploaded step-count algorithm on github the second version - means revised - version, or the original one?

Really basic question but maybe someone can help and we've overseen something.

Best
Katharina

