Oh, I see. You are expecting sleep analysis to be performed on a very short recording. I do  not think that is realistic with GGIR. GGIR assumes that there are at least midnights in the data as a reference point for nights.

I would advise exporting the epoch level features with part 1 and 2 and then processing the data outside GGIR. I recently wrote a script for someone with a similar request, although with no interest in sleep detection https://github.com/habitus-eu/hbGPS/blob/main/inst/postprocess_short_records.R So, this script does not do the sleep detection, but may provide you with a starting point.

And as I said:
> Good luck, this is my free advise if you want me to help write scripts then that would have to go via paid consultancy.

Best, Vincent

Dr. Vincent van Hees | Independent consultant | https://accelting.com/

